WEBVTT

00:32:30.450 --> 00:32:32.966
Before you challenge
organizational culture,

00:32:32.990 --> 00:32:35.363
it helps to demonstrate
your loyalty first.

00:32:36.240 --> 00:32:37.886
There's a special kind of status

00:32:37.910 --> 00:32:40.836
that allows you
to get away with nonconformity.

00:32:40.860 --> 00:32:43.976
In psychology, it's called
"idiosyncrasy credit."

00:32:44.000 --> 00:32:45.946
Once you prove your value to your group,

00:32:45.970 --> 00:32:49.506
you earn a license to deviate
from expectations.

00:32:49.530 --> 00:32:51.116
Research backs this up.

00:32:51.140 --> 00:32:52.571
A series of experiments show

00:32:52.595 --> 00:32:55.446
that trying to wield power
before earning status

00:32:55.470 --> 00:32:58.816
tends to breed conflict
with colleagues and superiors.

00:32:58.840 --> 00:33:01.346
When Carmen tried
to voice her authentic ideas,